          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Challenges of Transplantation</strong><br>\nThe success of the first heart transplant by Barnard brought both praise and criticism. While he became a symbol of medical innovation, he also faced the challenge of his patients' immune systems rejecting the new organs, which led to a continuous search for better immunosuppressive drugs.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Advancements in Cardiac Medicine</strong><br>\nBeyond transplantation, Barnard contributed to the development of cardiac surgery techniques. His work helped advance the understanding of congenital heart defects and he introduced new methods that improved the outcomes of heart surgery.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Global Medical Celebrity</strong><br>\nBarnard's achievement made him a celebrity in the medical community and beyond. He used his fame to promote medical advancements and became an outspoken figure on various health issues, advocating for better access to medical care.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
