            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Ethical and Social Impact</strong><br>\nThe procedures and ethical considerations introduced by Barnard's work in heart transplantation had profound implications. They prompted discussions on the definition of death, organ donation, and patients' rights, which influenced medical policy worldwide.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Career and Humanitarian Work</strong><br>\nLater in his career, Barnard focused on research and humanitarian efforts. He continued to practice medicine, teach, and write on medical topics, contributing to the broader understanding of health and diseases.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Christiaan Barnard</strong><br>\nChristiaan Barnard passed away in 2001, but his legacy endures. His work not only transformed the field of cardiac surgery but also inspired further innovations in organ transplantation. He left behind a legacy of medical breakthroughs that have saved countless lives.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
